{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>The inhabitants of the land.</b> They were its inhabitants before Esau came there. And our Rabbis interpreted (Shabbat 5): that they were expert in the settlement of the land — this stretch is fit for olives, this stretch is fit for vines — for they would taste the soil and know which planting was fit for it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:16.663264670Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}